<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Club</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. varied
Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>Clubs have been around for as long as mankind has walked erect (who can think of a caveman without picturing a club in his hand?). Styles of clubs range from simple sticks to elaborately carved works of art. Bashing weapons used to inflict concussion blows rather than piercing ones, clubs are effective against all opponents, armored or not. The most recent forms of the mace weapon are simply derivations of the club concept.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the club is a weapon skill of its own, one of the clubs and maces (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it bludgeons, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is of middling speed. It is taught by the barbarians from guild level 0, the fighters from guild level 0, the rangers from guild level 4, the thieves from guild level 4 (up to 80%), the knights from guild level 5, the paladins from guild level 5, the healers from guild level 6 (up to 70%), the druids from guild level 10 (up to 70%) and the necromancers from guild level 12 (up to 80%).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
